Travel full width at mid; map wide (maybe 1000px) and height ~640? SVG viewBox ratio 100:64 → at 1100 width height 704px! Too tall. Set `.chart{max-height:240px}` but SVG width 100% height auto; max-height distorts? With preserveAspectRatio default, max-height + width 100% will letterbox. Actually CSS max-height on SVG with width 100% and height auto sets width 100%, height ~640, then max-height clamps height but width remains 100% → aspect ratio distorted unless preserveAspectRatio meet (it will letterbox inside). It will show with blank side space. Fine. Better set `.chart-wrap{display:flex;justify-content:center}` and `.chart{max-width:520px}`. At full width, center chart at 520. Routes two columns. Do that.

Also at desktop 3-col, chart width ~360, height ~230. Good.

Journal full width at all sizes. At 901-1200 still spans.

At >1200, `.panel--journal` full width.

Header at 901-1200 top-actions maybe hide? HUD + brand + actions ~ 290+500+180 fits 900? At 950: brand 280 + hud 380 + actions 170 + gaps 56 = 886, tight. Set @media max-width 1100 `.top-actions{display:none}` and brand p hidden? Keep. Use 1200 breakpoint for actions hidden? Maybe show only at >1200. Do @media(max-width:1100){.top-actions{display:none}}.

Mobile landing: at 360, market table: good cell ~ 360-24 padding page=336 panel, td padding 8×2 ×5 columns=80; actions 96; good ~130; buy 36; sell 36; stock hidden = 298 + padding? Table auto. Tight but should fit. The actions cell with two buttons 40+3+40=83. Good cell may shrink, names wrap. Okay.

Topbar on mobile: HUD items. `hud-item--place` flex 1.4 with city name "Kestrel Point" might overflow; font 12; set text-overflow ellipsis? `.hud-item strong{white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;max-width:100%}`. HUD item min-width 0. Good. Hide rank.

Hide brand subtitle on very small (<420)? Maybe. Keep tiny.

