content.text:
Mobile buttons are now taller (34px), much better tap targets. The chips are 30px tall. But note the LOT chips "1 5 10 Max" and SHOW chips look better.

Issue: The market table is now clipped at "Salt" row by the tab bar; still a row is cut mid-way at the bottom, with faint content behind the tabbar. This is the fixed bar overlay. Because the page scrolls, that's typical, but the initial view ends mid-row. Could add a fade above the tab bar? The tab bar is fixed; can't put gradient above without another fixed element. Could add `box-shadow: 0 -12px 20px rgba(250,243,227,.9)`? A cleaner approach: give tabbar a solid background (it's .97 opacity + blur which shows content). Actually content is visible behind because the bar is translucent — "Salt" row and buttons are sliced and visible behind "MARKET ROAD CARAVAN JOURNAL". That looks a bit messy. Make the tabbar background more opaque (e.g., #f7eedb, solid) — but there will still be a hard cut at its top border. That's acceptable and standard for tab bars.

Better: Add a small fade strip above the tabbar via `.tabbar::before` fixed? `.tabbar` is fixed; pseudo-element position absolute top:-24px height 24px gradient from transparent to its bg. That softens the cut like desktop. Do:

```css
.tabbar::before {
  content:'';
  position:absolute;
  left:0; right:0; bottom:100%;
  height:22px;
  background: linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(247,238,219,0), rgba(247,238,219,.92));
  pointer-events:none;
}
```

But tabbar background is rgba(247,238,219,.97); gradient to that is fine. Yet the pseudo would cover the row softly — looks intentional.

Also, make tabbar background solid-ish: rgba(247,238,219,.98) is already near solid. The content visible behind is faint. With the pseudo fade, it'll look deliberate.

Another mobile issue: The "Sal" row's buttons are cut. After fade, fine.

Also: HUD "DAY 4" left, PURSE and LOCATION; rank hidden. Good.

Another mobile concern: the market table "BUY" values right aligned under header; header BUY at 227 vs values 221. Header labels have text-align left (they're th default left) — wait `.market-table th` has `text-align: left`. The `num` class is `text-align: right !important` — is it applied to th? In the screenshot, headers BUY, SELL, TRADE appear right-aligned: BUY at x~221-236, value 9 at 221... Actually header "BUY" spans 222-236, numbers "9" right edge 228. Hmm both look right-ish. Let me inspect the th markup in ui.js.

